<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anum-muttabbil</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 2000 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century-bce">21st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anum-muttabbil was a ruler of the Mesopotamian city of Der, east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a>, around the start of the 2nd millennium BCE. In an inscription he claimed to have struck down the heads of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anshan">Anshan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimashki-dynasty">Shimashki</a>, a boast that shows Der acting as an independent power on the Elamite frontier after the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-dynasty-of-ur">Third Dynasty of Ur</a>.</p></div>
